{
 "blocks": [
  {
   "id": 201,
   "voice": "N",
   "text": "In this town, nobody is allowed to look outside at exactly 2:17 AM. Nobody knows who made the rule. Nobody ever explains why. At 2:16, every curtain closes. And every light goes out.",
   "s": 0.05,
   "e": 10.232,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  },
  {
   "id": 202,
   "voice": "N",
   "text": "My name is Alex. And I always thought it was just a story to scare kids. Until last night. I was almost asleep... when I heard it.",
   "s": 10.382,
   "e": 16.786,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  },
  {
   "id": 203,
   "voice": "N",
   "text": "Three knocks. On my window. I checked the clock.",
   "s": 18.75,
   "e": 21.346,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  },
  {
   "id": 204,
   "voice": "N",
   "text": "Two seventeen. A.M.",
   "s": 22.85,
   "e": 24.472,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  },
  {
   "id": 205,
   "voice": "N",
   "text": "Then I heard my mom's voice. From outside.",
   "s": 24.672,
   "e": 27.033,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  },
  {
   "id": 301,
   "voice": "M",
   "text": "Alex... please... let me in.",
   "s": 27.183,
   "e": 29.973,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  },
  {
   "id": 206,
   "voice": "N",
   "text": "I looked. She was standing in the yard. Smiling. Same sweater. Same smile. But she didn't blink. Not once.",
   "s": 30.273,
   "e": 36.953,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  },
  {
   "id": 207,
   "voice": "N",
   "text": "Then a hand grabbed my shoulder. My real mom was standing behind me.",
   "s": 36.953,
   "e": 40.245,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  },
  {
   "id": 302,
   "voice": "W",
   "text": "Don't look at her.",
   "s": 40.345,
   "e": 42.305,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  },
  {
   "id": 208,
   "voice": "N",
   "text": "I turned back. But she was still there.",
   "s": 42.455,
   "e": 44.386,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  },
  {
   "id": 209,
   "voice": "N",
   "text": "The next morning, I looked outside. In front of every single house, someone was standing. Staring into the windows. And every single one of them... looked terrified.",
   "s": 44.386,
   "e": 53.411,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  },
  {
   "id": 210,
   "voice": "N",
   "text": "The rule was never protecting us from them. It was protecting them... from us.",
   "s": 54.161,
   "e": 58.466,
   "src": "higgsfield"
  }
 ],
